","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_pack_018_domain_new_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which input is excluded from the domain of $f(x)=1/(x-3)$?","options":["$0$","$1$","$-3$","$3$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7507d77f74b8f73bccceb3d4","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_pack_018_domain_new_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which function has all real numbers as its usual domain?","options":["$f(x)=1/x$","$f(x)=\\sqrt{x}$","$f(x)=x^2+1$","$f(x)=1/(x-1)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"75b0766bd595f9df558aaae7","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_pack_018_domain_new_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What is the natural real domain of $f(x)=\\sqrt{1-x}$?","options":["$[1,+\\infty)$","$\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{1\\}$","$(-\\infty,1]$","$(0,1)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0ffa57cf700504dfad777aaf","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_domain_e626300b_003_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"With the usual convention (largest set of real inputs on which the formula makes sense), what is the domain of $f(x)=\\sqrt{9-x^2}$?","options":["$[-3,3]$","$[0,3]$","$(-3,3)$","$(-\\infty,-3]\\cup[3,+\\infty)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a12408322719034a6ccb532b","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_domain_e626300b_008_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"With the usual convention (largest set of real inputs on which the formula makes sense), what is the domain of $f(x)=x^{2/3}=(\\sqrt[3]{x})^2$?","options":["$\\mathbb{R}$","$[0,+\\infty)$","$(0,+\\infty)$","$\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"048182acf821ad676f1e026d","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_domain_e626300b_topup20261028_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"With the usual convention (largest set of real inputs on which the formula makes sense), what is the domain of $f(x)=\\dfrac{\\ln x}{x-1}$?","options":["$[0,1)\\cup(1,+\\infty)$","$(0,1)\\cup(1,+\\infty)$","$(0,+\\infty)$","$\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{1\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"525202981c202cee21a34343","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_domain_e626300b_topup20261028_002","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f(x)=1/x$ on $\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$ and $g(y)=\\sqrt{y-1}$ on $[1,+\\infty)$. What is the largest set $D\\subseteq\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$ such that every value $f(x)$ with $x\\in D$ lies in the domain of $g$, so that $g\\circ f$ is defined on $D$?","options":["$[1,+\\infty)$","$\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$","$(-\\infty,0)\\cup(0,1]$","$(0,1]$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"18e3c5804b9bfe713f041d5e","time_limit":35}]}}